---
description: Backend, server, and shared logic rules
globs: ["server/**/*.ts", "src/lib/**/*.ts"]
---

Backend rules:
- keep route, handler, and controller logic thin when possible
- move reusable business logic into dedicated modules
- isolate external API calls and provider-specific code
- validate external input
- avoid hidden side effects
- prefer explicit data flow and explicit return shapes
- preserve existing contracts unless explicitly changing them
- prefer minimal safe diffs over architectural rewrites

When changing server logic:
- first identify the current execution flow
- preserve working behavior
- make failure paths and async behavior easier to understand